er Intramurals Roos House Directory Faculty/Staff Directory Office Contacts Quick Links SUNY Canton OnLine Brightspace (D2L) Brightspace Info Center Email UCanWeb Accommodate Canton Rave Alert System Handshake International Programs RooLife RooSuccess Weather Update Facebook Instagram LinkedIn TikTok X/Twitter YouTube Faculty/Staff Directory Office Contacts About Canton Academic Degrees Admissions Campus Forms Campus Store Course Listings Employment Env. Health & Safety Financial Aid Human Resources Information Services Learning Commons Library Online Payment Placement Testing President's Office Provost's Office Registrar Special Events Student Accounts (Billing) Textbooks University Police Home > Human Resources > Job Opportunities > Faculty > Assistant Professor - Applied Psychology Assistant Professor - Applied Psychology Faculty Position TITLE: Assistant Professor - Applied Psychology DEPARTMENT: Applied Psychology SALARY RANGE: $63,000 - $68,000 Description of Duties The State University of New York (SUNY) College at Canton invites qualified applicants for a full-time, Tenure-Track Assistant Professor position in the Applied Psychology Department beginning fall, 2027. Responsibilities A 4/4 teaching load, which will include face-to-face courses, plus the use of online, hybrid, and converged modalities. Teaching assignments may include courses in Introductory Psychology, Research Methods, Cultural Psychology, Personality, Professional Ethics, Counseling Skills among others depending on area of expertise. Advising and mentoring students. Collaborative participation in course, curriculum, program development, and assessment. Participation in campus, university, and community service activities. Engagement in professional development and relevant scholarly activity. Demonstrated commitment to scholarly activity, including an active research agenda, a record (or strong potential) of publications presentations, and a willingness to engage students in research, creative work, or other scholarly pursuits. Qualifications Required: PhD in psychology or DSW (ABD acceptable with plan for graduation) or equivalent. Preferred: Other Ranks Considered: Master's degree also considered and meets requirements for Instructor rank. Prior to a final offer of employment, the selected candidate will be required to submit to a background check including, but not limited to, employment verification, educational and other credential verification, and criminal background check. Closing Date for Receipt of Applications Review begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. Apply for Position SUNY Canton does not discriminate based on race, color, national origin, sex, gender identity, disability, or age in its education programs, services, and activities, including employment policies and practices. Human Resources Administrative Services Human Resources Forms Policies & Procedures Labor Contracts Ethics Guidelines Alternate Work Schedules  Top 34 Cornell Drive Canton, NY 13617 Admissions Students Faculty Academics Alumni Community Athletics Academic Programs | Tuition & Fees Brightspace | Financial Aid | Library | UCanWeb CLDIOI | College Assembly | Email | UCanWeb Catalog | Course Descriptions | Majors | Registrar Foundation | Reunion | Transcripts Directions | Police Academy | SBDC Fitness Center | Intramurals Stay Connected 315-386-7011 1-800-388-7123 © 2026 SUNY Canton | Web Accessibility | Privacy Statement | Non-Discrimination/Title IX"
