tramurals Roos House Directory Faculty/Staff Directory Office Contacts Quick Links SUNY Canton OnLine Brightspace (D2L) Brightspace Info Center Email UCanWeb Accommodate Canton Rave Alert System Handshake International Programs RooLife RooSuccess Weather Update Facebook Instagram LinkedIn TikTok X/Twitter YouTube Faculty/Staff Directory Office Contacts About Canton Academic Degrees Admissions Campus Forms Campus Store Course Listings Employment Env. Health & Safety Financial Aid Human Resources Information Services Learning Commons Library Online Payment Placement Testing President's Office Provost's Office Registrar Special Events Student Accounts (Billing) Textbooks University Police Home > Human Resources > Job Opportunities > Faculty > Assistant Professor - Legal Studies Assistant Professor - Legal Studies Faculty Position TITLE: Assistant Professor - Legal Studies DEPARTMENT: Humanities SALARY RANGE: $65,000 - $70,000 Description of Duties The State University of New York (SUNY) College at Canton invites qualified applicants for a full-time, Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Legal Studies faculty position in the Humanities Department beginning September 1, 2027. Responsibilities - Qualifications Required: A Juris Doctor Degree. Ability to develop and deliver law courses across online, face-to-face, and flex (hybrid) modalities. Ability to teach undergraduate-level courses, focused on tax law, income tax, and individual taxation. Ability to teach a wide-range of undergraduate-level law courses, including business law, environmental law, immigration law, criminal practice, civil litigation, legal research, and legal writing. Strong commitment to academic mentoring and student development. Preferred: Admission to state bar. At least 5 years of experience practicing law. Prior teaching experience in college-level courses. D. Degree. Experience integrating applied learning into curriculum design and instruction. Demonstrated excellence in teaching, with a proven ability to engage and inspire students in both traditional and online settings. Proven ability to work effectively with a diverse student body, including non-traditional and first-generation college students. Proven ability to work effectively with a diverse student body, including non-traditional and first-generation college students. Other Ranks Considered Prior to a final offer of employment, the selected candidate will be required to submit to a background check including, but not limited to, employment verification, educational and other credential verification, and criminal background check. Closing Date for Receipt of Applications Review begins immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Apply for Position SUNY Canton does not discriminate based on race, color, national origin, sex, gender identity, disability, or age in its education programs, services, and activities, including employment policies and practices. Human Resources Administrative Services Human Resources Forms Policies & Procedures Labor Contracts Ethics Guidelines Alternate Work Schedules  Top 34 Cornell Drive Canton, NY 13617 Admissions Students Faculty Academics Alumni Community Athletics Academic Programs | Tuition & Fees Brightspace | Financial Aid | Library | UCanWeb CLDIOI | College Assembly | Email | UCanWeb Catalog | Course Descriptions | Majors | Registrar Foundation | Reunion | Transcripts Directions | Police Academy | SBDC Fitness Center | Intramurals Stay Connected 315-386-7011 1-800-388-7123 © 2026 SUNY Canton | Web Accessibility | Privacy Statement | Non-Discrimination/Title IX"
