er Intramurals Roos House Directory Faculty/Staff Directory Office Contacts Quick Links SUNY Canton OnLine Brightspace (D2L) Brightspace Info Center Email UCanWeb Accommodate Canton Rave Alert System Handshake International Programs RooLife RooSuccess Weather Update Facebook Instagram LinkedIn TikTok X/Twitter YouTube Faculty/Staff Directory Office Contacts About Canton Academic Degrees Admissions Campus Forms Campus Store Course Listings Employment Env. Health & Safety Financial Aid Human Resources Information Services Learning Commons Library Online Payment Placement Testing President's Office Provost's Office Registrar Special Events Student Accounts (Billing) Textbooks University Police Home > Human Resources > Job Opportunities > Faculty > Assistant Professor – Veterinary Science Assistant Professor – Veterinary Science Faculty Position TITLE: Assistant Professor – Veterinary Science DEPARTMENT: Veterinary Science Technology and Veterinary Service Administration SALARY RANGE: $67,000 - $70,000 Description of Duties The State University of New York (SUNY) College at Canton invites qualified applicants for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor position in the Veterinary Science Technology and Veterinary Service Administration Departments beginning January 1, 2027. Responsibilities Duties: Classroom instruction and in-person laboratory instruction, including but not limited to small and large animal veterinary nursing labs, small animal surgical labs, clinical pathology labs, radiology labs, anatomy and physiology labs, and lead instruction on other courses as needed. Academic advising for students, as well as student club advising, is also required. Assistance with development of new curriculum and educational opportunities is also a requirement. Participation in faculty committees and other activities related to university service and engagement in scholarly activities that contribute to the dissemination of knowledge in the discipline is also required. Qualifications Required Qualifications: DVM/VMD required. NY state licensure required. Documents needed with application: CV, cover letter, statement of teaching philosophy, statement of research, unofficial transcripts, statement of diversity, equity, and inclusion, and three professional references. Prior to a final offer of employment, the selected candidate will be required to submit to a background check including, but not limited to, employment verification, educational and other credential verification, and criminal background check. Closing Date for Receipt of Applications Review begins immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Apply for Position SUNY Canton does not discriminate based on race, color, national origin, sex, gender identity, disability, or age in its education programs, services, and activities, including employment policies and practices. Human Resources Administrative Services Human Resources Forms Policies & Procedures Labor Contracts Ethics Guidelines Alternate Work Schedules  Top 34 Cornell Drive Canton, NY 13617 Admissions Students Faculty Academics Alumni Community Athletics Academic Programs | Tuition & Fees Brightspace | Financial Aid | Library | UCanWeb CLDIOI | College Assembly | Email | UCanWeb Catalog | Course Descriptions | Majors | Registrar Foundation | Reunion | Transcripts Directions | Police Academy | SBDC Fitness Center | Intramurals Stay Connected 315-386-7011 1-800-388-7123 © 2026 SUNY Canton | Web Accessibility | Privacy Statement | Non-Discrimination/Title IX"
