irectory Faculty/Staff Directory Office Contacts Quick Links SUNY Canton OnLine Brightspace (D2L) Brightspace Info Center Email UCanWeb Accommodate Canton Rave Alert System Handshake International Programs RooLife RooSuccess Weather Update Facebook Instagram LinkedIn TikTok X/Twitter YouTube Faculty/Staff Directory Office Contacts About Canton Academic Degrees Admissions Campus Forms Campus Store Course Listings Employment Env. Health & Safety Financial Aid Human Resources Information Services Learning Commons Library Online Payment Placement Testing President's Office Provost's Office Registrar Special Events Student Accounts (Billing) Textbooks University Police Home > Human Resources > Job Opportunities > Faculty > HVAC Lecturer Lecturer, HVAC Faculty Position TITLE: Lecturer, HVAC DEPARTMENT: Mechanical and Energy Systems, CSOET SALARY RANGE: $50,000 - $65,000 Description of Duties The State University of New York (SUNY) College at Canton invites qualified applicants for a full-time Lecturer position in the HVAC Department, beginning August 24, 2026. Responsibilities An educator who is passionate about hands-on teaching and committed to student success. The ideal candidate will bring professional expertise in multiple areas of HVAC service, including (but not limited to): Electrical HVAC systems, residential and commercial refrigeration, heating systems (forced air and hydronics), and plumbing systems. Teach face-to-face lecture and laboratory courses – with occasional remote instruction on designated snow days. Advise, mentor, and support students across a range of academic ability levels. Participate in curriculum development, promote assessment, and continuous improvement initiatives. Contribute to department, college, and community service; including committee work and outreach. Foster a learning environment that promotes diversity, equity, inclusion, and accessibility. Collaborate with faculty and industry partners to keep the curriculum aligned with current HVAC workforce needs. Qualifications Required: Associate’s degree in HVAC with a minimum of three years of professional HVAC industry experience; or degree equivalent with eight years of professional HVAC experience. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Preferred: Bachelor’s degree or higher in a related technical discipline. Prior teaching, training, or instructional experience (college, high school, or industry-based). Prior to a final offer of employment, the selected candidate will be required to submit to a background check including, but not limited to, employment verification, educational and other credential verification, and criminal background check. Closing Date for Receipt of Applications Review begins immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Apply for Position SUNY Canton does not discriminate based on race, color, national origin, sex, gender identity, disability, or age in its education programs, services, and activities, including employment policies and practices. Human Resources Administrative Services Human Resources Forms Policies & Procedures Labor Contracts Ethics Guidelines Alternate Work Schedules  Top 34 Cornell Drive Canton, NY 13617 Admissions Students Faculty Academics Alumni Community Athletics Academic Programs | Tuition & Fees Brightspace | Financial Aid | Library | UCanWeb CLDIOI | College Assembly | Email | UCanWeb Catalog | Course Descriptions | Majors | Registrar Foundation | Reunion | Transcripts Directions | Police Academy | SBDC Fitness Center | Intramurals Stay Connected 315-386-7011 1-800-388-7123 © 2026 SUNY Canton | Web Accessibility | Privacy Statement | Non-Discrimination/Title IX"
